  "configuration_id": "config_038",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_036 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, weighted) achieved 0.706 accuracy, dramatically outperforming all scgpt-based configs (~0.52-0.54), establishing scvi_n200 as the dominant RNA encoder. The remaining uncertainty is whether transformer aggregation can further improve upon avgpool with this stronger encoder. Question tested: config_038 isolates the aggregation axis (avgpool→transformer) while holding the proven scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + weighted fusion stack constant. With scgpt, transformer was slightly worse (0.520 vs 0.542), but scvi_n200 produces a richer latent representation where learned attention over profiles may capture interactions that simple averaging misses. Why this is the best next experiment: it is a single-variable, high-information test around the current best configuration, directly informing whether to exploit transformer aggregation in subsequent runs or confirm avgpool as optimal. Expected cost: ~4.7–5.0 GPU hours (comparable to config_036's 4.82, since transformer vs avgpool showed negligible cost difference in the scgpt comparisons), keeping total budget well within limits with 5 experiments remaining."
}

